Bard wrote:
> As several players have said recently, Nethack is a little dull when
> you realize that virtually everything you need for the standard AK is
> handed to you.
>
> Here's a list of ideas that have occured to me over the past couple
> weeks of playing that might make NetHack a little more interesting and
> challenging without greatly altering the game from its roots.
>

> 3. Wand of Wishing is NOT guaranteed at the castle. Wishes are nice,
> but at the point you get this wand of wishing  it's either far too
> useful (i.e. you pretty much know what you're lacking and you can wish
> for it) or it's pretty much unnecessary ("ho-hum I found most of my
> kit already what else can I wish for?").
>
> Alternative: It'd be better, in my opinion, if you really wanted to
> have a guaranteed wand of wishing to include it early in the game,
> when the players can be torn between whether they need to use it or
> whether they should hold off. Perhaps the Oracle has a guaranteed
> Wand of Wishing on her exalted person? ;)
>


Putting a /oW doesn't make the game harder, I would say it makes it 
significantly easier.  It's not like there are an over abundance of stuff 
that is only useful in the early game, or things that are only useful in the 
late game (For example, speed boots, (S|G)DSM, CoMR, are all pretty useful 
in both the early and late games)

I mean, if the oracle had a /oW, I'd find a way to kill her or die trying in 
every game, and wish up my AK. 




